{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LANDING STATUS — core fix MERGED, parity follow-up in review.\n\nChange #2399 (rebar-ticket 1137, attest.py unscoped whole-HEAD arm + RED->GREEN oracle) is MERGED to origin/main at c0be6c257f5a with LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1. This resolves the primary defect (foreign stale-head permanently blocking claim on epic/file_impact-less plan-review) and unblocks the epic claim that was waiting on it.\n\nParity follow-up change #2401 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2401, rebar-ticket 1137) extracts the single shared anchor helper gate_source.current_head_sha and routes BOTH attest._unscoped_head_drift and drift_floor's code_drifted read through it, so the two intentionally-synchronized unscoped-HEAD anchors cannot diverge (addresses the plan-review G6 finding and folds in sibling 3409). make lint + make typecheck clean; modules <=800 LOC (gate_source 272, attest 794, drift_floor 349); complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0; 2391 unit tests pass. Awaiting LLM-Review + Verified on #2401 before self-submit; will close this ticket (all 5 file_impact paths landed) and 3409 after #2401 merges."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788051575312185001,"uuid":"c8cf1d0c-c890-46ff-97d3-e5f68097f6c1"}